        "heading": "A family weaving workshop at the pedal loom",
        "heading_size": "h2",
        "body": "<p>In a family-run workshop, spinning, dyeing and weaving are shared within the family. They weave on the pedal loom: feet set the warp, hands pass the shuttle. Patterns are kept in memory, so even with the same design, no two pieces are identical.</p><p>Every colour is naturally dyed: reds and pinks from cochineal, blues from indigo, yellows and oranges from pericón and marigold, browns from walnut.</p>",
